      "hints": [
        "Find $x$ term: $\\binom{7}{1}(2^6)(ax) = 448ax$.",
        "Find $x^2$ term: $\\binom{7}{2}(2^5)(a^2x^2) = 672a^2x^2$.",
        "Equate coefficients $448a = 672a^2 \\implies a = \\frac{448}{672} = \\frac{2}{3}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write the general term $T_{r+1}$ in the binomial expansion of $(2 + ax)^7$:\n$$T_{r+1} = \\binom{7}{r}2^{7-r}(ax)^r = \\binom{7}{r}2^{7-r}a^r x^r$$",
        "Extract the terms in $x$ (for $r = 1$) and $x^2$ (for $r = 2$):\n$$\\text{Term in } x = \\binom{7}{1}2^6 a x = 7(64)a x = 448a x$$\n$$\\text{Term in } x^2 = \\binom{7}{2}2^5 a^2 x^2 = 21(32)a^2 x^2 = 672a^2 x^2$$",
        "Equate the two coefficients and solve for $a \\ne 0$:\n$$448a = 672a^2 \\implies 672a = 448 \\implies a = \\frac{448}{672} = \\frac{2}{3} \\quad (\\approx 0.667)$$"
      ],
